# Day 1 - Unreal C++ Setup

## What I did today

- Installed Unreal Engine 5
- Installed Visual Studio 2022 with Game development with C++
- Created a C++ Third Person Unreal project
- Opened the project in Visual Studio
- Compiled the project
- Pressed Play in Unreal
- Added a C++ debug message on screen
- Started Git/GitHub tracking

## What I learned

- Unreal C++ projects use Visual Studio to compile code.
- BeginPlay runs when the actor starts in the game world.
- GEngine->AddOnScreenDebugMessage can print debug text on screen.
- Blueprint is not bad. C++ and Blueprint can work together.

